<title>UK: Cathay drops ex-UK cargo surcharge May 1.</title>
<headline>Cathay drops ex-UK cargo surcharge May 1.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cathay Pacific Airways Ltd says it will drop its ex-UK cargo fuel surcharge with effect from May 1.</p>
<p>The surcharge of five pence a kg was introduced on November 25.</p>
<p>Cathay's cargo manager, north UK , Ivor Llewellyn told Reuters that the decision only applied to ex-UK routes.</p>
<p>Yesterday Lufthansa Cargo announced that it was scrapping its surcharge with effect from April 15 and Dutch shippers have been told that KLM Royal Dutch Airlines NV is expected to make a similar move on the same day.</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542-7706 Fax+5017</p>
